  "attack_progression": [
    {"step": 1, "tactic": "Credential Access — Password Spraying", "technique": "T1110.003", "what_happened": "At 2026-03-10 01:02:14 UTC, the SSL-VPN portal (10.108.57.10, /remote/login) began receiving authentication failures from a single external source data.srcip=185.220.101.45 (User-Agent 'FortiClient/7.2.4 Windows'). Phase 1 of the spray walked a BROAD username list — admin, administrator, service.desk, vpn.user, help.desk, security.ops — each tried against a small set of common passwords ('Welcome2025!', 'Summer25Pass!'). The operator inserted 25-45s of jitter between every attempt and a ~55s pause between password rounds, deliberately staying under the per-account lockout threshold. Wazuh rule 5710 'Multiple authentication failures from same source IP' fired.", "chain_reason": "Wazuh rule 5710 correlated >=6 failed VPN auth events sharing data.srcip=185.220.101.45 against data.dstip=10.108.57.10 within a rolling window, each event carrying a distinct data.win.eventdata.targetUserName. Single external source + many usernames + low password count = password spray, not single-account brute force.", "first_seen": "2026-03-10T01:02:14+0000"},
    {"step": 2, "tactic": "Credential Access — Password Spraying (focused)", "technique": "T1110.003", "what_happened": "At ~01:09 UTC the same data.srcip=185.220.101.45 narrowed to a focused contractor-account list — contractor.smith, contractor.jones, ext.contractor — and tried three more passwords ('Corp2024!', 'Admin@123', 'ChangeMe2024!'). The shift from broad role-account names to specific contractor accounts indicates the operator had refined the target list, consistent with prior reconnaissance of the org's identity namespace. Sustained failure volume tripped Wazuh rule 5711 'VPN credential spray detected (>4 failures/min)'.", "chain_reason": "Wazuh rule 5711 fired on aggregate VPN auth-failure rate from data.srcip=185.220.101.45 exceeding the >4/min threshold, with data.win.eventdata.targetUserName cycling across the contractor.* namespace. The phase-2 target-list refinement is the operator-skill marker distinguishing this from an automated credential-stuffing bot.", "first_seen": "2026-03-10T01:09:02+0000"},
    {"step": 3, "tactic": "Initial Access — External Remote Services", "technique": "T1133", "what_happened": "At 2026-03-10 01:18:47 UTC, after ~16 minutes of failures, a SUCCESSFUL VPN authentication was recorded for data.win.eventdata.targetUserName=contractor.smith from the SAME data.srcip=185.220.101.45 — the spray landed. The successful login carried Windows Security event 4624 semantics (interactive remote logon) and was immediately followed by VPN session-cookie creation. MFA was NOT enforced on this contractor account (password-only authentication), so the single correct credential was sufficient for full network access. This converts the incident from 'failed spray' to 'confirmed external foothold'.", "chain_reason": "A data.win.eventdata.targetUserName=contractor.smith success event (Windows eventID 4624 equivalent) shares data.srcip=185.220.101.45 with the preceding 5710/5711 failure burst, within the same continuous time window. Same-source failure-burst-then-success is the canonical password-spray-success signature; T1133 attaches because the access vector is the external VPN service.", "first_seen": "2026-03-10T01:18:47+0000"},
    {"step": 4, "tactic": "Initial Access — Correlated Alert", "technique": "T1133", "what_happened": "Across the 01:02-01:20 UTC window (~18 min), Wazuh aggregated ~38 VPN authentication events from data.srcip=185.220.101.45 against the VPN portal 10.108.57.10 — 37 failures spanning 9 distinct usernames plus 1 success on contractor.smith. The combined signature (single non-corporate external source + many usernames + lockout-avoidance jitter + a terminal success on a contractor account with no MFA) is the canonical password-spray-into-external-remote-services chain that MITRE T1110.003 + T1133 describe.", "chain_reason": "Wazuh correlation rule 'VPN credential spray with successful authentication' fired on the combination of rule 5710 + rule 5711 + a success event, all sharing data.srcip=185.220.101.45 and data.dstip=10.108.57.10 within an 18-minute window. The MITRE mapping T1110.003 (Password Spraying) + T1133 (External Remote Services) was attached automatically by the rule.", "first_seen": "2026-03-10T01:20:39+0000"}
  ],
